ng_btsocket_sco: SCO and eSCO parameters; send one packet at a time

HFP's Audio Gateway (bluetoothd) has to choose the air coding (CVSD, or
transparent for mSBC wide-band speech), packet types, latency and
retransmission effort of each synchronous link, and SCO sockets could
only ask for a legacy SCO link.

- SO_SCO_SYNC_PARAMS (set before connect() or listen()) makes connect()
  send NGM_HCI_LP_SYNC_CON_REQ, and the answer to an incoming request
  NGM_HCI_LP_SYNC_CON_RSP, with the socket's parameters; an accepted
  socket inherits the listener's. Without it nothing changes.
- SO_SCO_SYNC_INFO returns what the controller negotiated, from
  NGM_HCI_LP_SYNC_CON_INFO.
- The state rides behind each PCB (struct ng_btsocket_sco_pcb_ext), so
  struct ng_btsocket_sco_pcb keeps its layout. The options, messages and
  state are in ng_btsocket_sco_sync.[ch] (this directory's src/), the
  messages in NgHCI's ng_hci_sync_lp.h.
- ng_btsocket_sco_send2() sent the first queued record over and over
  until the route's SCO buffers were full, while its callers keep one
  packet in flight and drop one record per completed packet; it never
  sent at all on a controller that reports no SCO buffers. Send one.

Origin: NextBSD (nextbsd/nextbsd-kernel#237). Not upstream.
Applies to: releng/15.1 sys/netgraph/bluetooth/socket/ng_btsocket_sco.c

